---
.title = "Docker launch",
.description = "Download a checkpoint to your home directory or load it from Hugging Face when LLMD starts. Configure Docker and LLMD flags for your launch.",
.date = .date("2026-11-17T00:00:00"),
.layout = "content.shtml",
---
Run the commands on your Docker host. Check the exact checkpoint, backend,
and image in [Supported Models]($link.page('llmd/models')). For restricted
repositories, see [Hugging Face credentials]($link.page('reference/environment').ref('model-storage-and-credentials')).

```=html
<div class="llmd-launch" data-llmd-launch>
  <div id="lfm3-fp8-cuda"></div>
  <div id="lfm3-fp8-rocm"></div>
  <div id="lfm3-oneapi"></div>
  <div id="qwen3-8-27b-cuda"></div>
  <div id="qwen3-8-27b-rocm"></div>
  <div id="qwen3-8-27b-oneapi"></div>
  <noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to apply a catalog preset. The example below uses Gemma 4 with CUDA.</p></noscript>
  <div class="llmd-launch-layout">
    <form class="llmd-launch-settings" data-pagefind-ignore hidden>
      <fieldset class="command-tabs" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-source-hint">
        <legend>Model source</legend>
        <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="source" value="download" checked><span>Download first</span></label>
        <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="source" value="local"><span>Already downloaded</span></label>
        <label class="command-tab"><input type="radio" name="source" value="hub"><span>Load at launch</span></label>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-source-hint" data-hint></span>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="llmd-launch-field">
        <label for="llmd-launch-checkpoint">Checkpoint</label>
        <select id="llmd-launch-checkpoint" name="checkpoint" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-checkpoint-hint">
          <option>google/gemma-4-31B-it</option>
          <option>meta-llama/Llama-3.1-8B-Instruct</option>
          <option>Qwen/Qwen3.5-9B</option>
          <option>Qwen/Qwen3.5-35B-A3B</option>
          <option>Qwen/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-FP8</option>
          <option>Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B</option>
          <option>Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B-FP8</option>
          <option>google/gemma-4-12B-it</option>
          <option>LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B</option>
          <option>google/gemma-4-26B-A4B-it</option>
          <option>meta-models/Muse-Glimmer-30B</option>
          <option>poolside/Laguna-XS-2.1</option>
          <option>LiquidAI/LFM3-1.7B-FP8</option>
        </select>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-checkpoint-hint">Choose a Hugging Face checkpoint from the list.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="llmd-launch-field" data-local>
        <label for="llmd-launch-directory">Host checkpoint directory</label>
        <input id="llmd-launch-directory" name="directory" type="text" value="${HOME}/models/google/gemma-4-31B-it" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-directory-hint llmd-launch-directory-error">
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-directory-hint">Use a subdirectory such as ${HOME}/models/org/checkpoint. Omit <code>..</code> and trailing spaces.</span>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-directory-error" data-field-error="directory" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
      <div class="llmd-launch-field" data-revision>
        <label for="llmd-launch-revision">Checkpoint commit</label>
        <input id="llmd-launch-revision" name="revision" type="text" placeholder="Optional commit SHA" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-revision-hint llmd-launch-revision-error">
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-revision-hint">Use a 40-character hexadecimal SHA, or leave blank for the default revision.</span>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-revision-error" data-field-error="revision" aria-live="polite"></span>
      </div>
      <div data-hub hidden>
        <label class="llmd-launch-checkbox">
          <input name="hfToken" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-token-hint"> Forward <code>HF_TOKEN</code>
        </label>
        <p class="llmd-launch-hint" id="llmd-launch-token-hint">Check to pass the host's Hugging Face token to Docker.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="llmd-launch-field">
        <label for="llmd-launch-backend">Backend</label>
        <select id="llmd-launch-backend" name="backend" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-backend-hint">
          <option value="cuda">NVIDIA CUDA</option>
          <option value="rocm">AMD ROCm</option>
          <option value="oneapi">Intel oneAPI</option>
        </select>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-backend-hint">Choose CUDA, ROCm, or oneAPI to match your GPU.</span>
      </div>
      <div data-dspine hidden>
        <label class="llmd-launch-checkbox">
          <input name="dspine" type="checkbox" aria-describedby="llmd-dspine-hint" disabled> DSpine speculative decoding
        </label>
        <p class="llmd-launch-hint" id="llmd-dspine-hint">Off by default. Enabling DSpine sets batch size to 1.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="llmd-launch-field" data-drafter-source hidden>
        <label for="llmd-launch-drafter-source">Drafter source</label>
        <select id="llmd-launch-drafter-source" name="drafterSource" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-drafter-source-hint" disabled>
          <option value="hub">Hugging Face at launch</option>
          <option value="local">Mount local drafter</option>
        </select>
        <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-drafter-source-hint">Load from Hugging Face or mount the drafter from the Docker host.</span>
      </div>
      <details class="llmd-launch-options" open>
        <summary>Launch options</summary>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>Docker flags</legend>
          <div class="llmd-launch-options-grid">
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-port">Host port</label>
              <input id="llmd-launch-port" name="port" type="text" inputmode="numeric" value="8000" aria-required="true" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-port-hint llmd-launch-port-error">
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-port-hint">Whole number from 1 to 65535.</span>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-port-error" data-field-error="port" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-run-mode">Run mode</label>
              <select id="llmd-launch-run-mode" name="runMode" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-run-mode-hint">
                <option value="foreground">Foreground</option>
                <option value="detached">Detached</option>
              </select>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-run-mode-hint">Foreground attaches to the container. Detached runs in the background.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field" data-cuda>
              <label for="llmd-launch-gpu">GPU access</label>
              <select id="llmd-launch-gpu" name="gpu" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-gpu-hint">
                <option value="all">All GPUs</option>
                <option value="device=0">GPU 0</option>
              </select>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-gpu-hint">Expose all CUDA GPUs or only GPU 0.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-shm">Shared memory</label>
              <select id="llmd-launch-shm" name="shm" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-shm-hint">
                <option value="recipe">Recipe setting</option>
                <option value="default">Docker default</option>
                <option value="1g">1 GiB</option>
                <option value="8g">8 GiB</option>
                <option value="32g">32 GiB</option>
                <option value="256g">256 GiB</option>
              </select>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-shm-hint">Use the recipe or Docker default, or choose 1, 8, 32, or 256 GiB.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
        <fieldset>
          <legend>LLMD overrides</legend>
          <div class="llmd-launch-options-grid">
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-context">Context tokens</label>
              <input id="llmd-launch-context" name="context" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="Image default" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-context-hint llmd-launch-context-error">
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-context-hint">Whole number from 1 to 4,294,967,295, or blank.</span>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-context-error" data-field-error="context" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field" data-batch>
              <label for="llmd-launch-batch">Batch size</label>
              <input id="llmd-launch-batch" name="batch" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="Image default" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-batch-hint llmd-launch-batch-error">
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-batch-hint">Whole number from 1 to 4,294,967,295, or blank.</span>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-batch-error" data-field-error="batch" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-tokens">Token batch size</label>
              <input id="llmd-launch-tokens" name="tokens" type="text" inputmode="numeric" placeholder="Image default" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-tokens-hint llmd-launch-tokens-error">
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-tokens-hint">Whole number from 1 to 4,294,967,295, or blank.</span>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-tokens-error" data-field-error="tokens" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
            <div class="llmd-launch-field">
              <label for="llmd-launch-memory">GPU memory fraction</label>
              <input id="llmd-launch-memory" name="memory" type="text" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="Image default" aria-describedby="llmd-launch-memory-hint llmd-launch-memory-error">
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-hint" id="llmd-launch-memory-hint">Decimal greater than 0 and at most 1, such as 0.5, or blank.</span>
              <span class="llmd-launch-field-error" id="llmd-launch-memory-error" data-field-error="memory" aria-live="polite"></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </details>
    </form>
    <div class="llmd-launch-commands">
      <p class="llmd-launch-error" role="status" data-error data-pagefind-ignore hidden>Correct the fields with errors to generate the launch and API commands.</p>
      <section data-download-step>
        <h2>Download checkpoint</h2>
        <div class="command-shell">
          <span class="command-language icon-code">Host shell</span>
          <pre><code class="sh" data-command="download">uvx --from huggingface_hub hf download google/gemma-4-31B-it \
  --local-dir "${HOME:?Set HOME to your absolute home directory}"/models/google/gemma-4-31B-it
</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section data-drafter-download-step hidden>
        <h2>Download DSpine drafter</h2>
        <p class="llmd-launch-hint">Download once on the Docker host, or reuse an existing copy at this path.</p>
        <div class="command-shell">
          <span class="command-language icon-code">Host shell</span>
          <pre><code class="sh" data-command="drafter-download"></code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Launch LLMD</h2>
        <p class="llmd-launch-hint" data-recipe>The published Gemma CUDA recipe uses the rolling image with DFlash.</p>
        <div class="command-shell" data-launch-output>
          <span class="command-language icon-code">Host shell</span>
          <pre><code class="sh" data-command="launch">(
  model_dir="${HOME:?Set HOME to your absolute home directory}"/models/google/gemma-4-31B-it
  case "$model_dir" in
    /*) ;;
    *) printf '%s\n' 'HOME must be an absolute path.' >&amp;2; exit 1 ;;
  esac
  model_src=$(printf '%s' "$model_dir" | sed 's/"/""/g') || exit 1
  docker run --rm --name llmd \
    -p 127.0.0.1:8000:8000 \
    --gpus=all \
    --shm-size=256GB \
    --mount "type=bind,\"source=${model_src}\",target=/model,readonly" \
    zmlai/llmd:cuda \
    --model=/model \
    --model-name=gemma-4-31B-it
)
</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>
      <section data-models-step>
        <h2>Check the loaded model</h2>
        <p>After LLMD finishes loading, run this in a second terminal on the Docker host.</p>
        <div class="command-shell">
          <span class="command-language icon-code">Host shell</span>
          <pre><code class="sh" data-command="models">curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/models</code></pre>
        </div>
        <p>Confirm that <code>data[0].id</code> in the response is <code data-expected-model-id>gemma-4-31B-it</code>.</p>
      </section>
      <section data-chat-step>
        <h2>Send a first chat request</h2>
        <p>After the model check succeeds, run this in the same terminal. Look for <code>choices[0].message.content</code> in the response.</p>
        <div class="command-shell">
          <span class="command-language icon-code">Host shell</span>
          <pre><code class="sh" data-command="chat">curl -fsS http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{
    "model": "gemma-4-31B-it",
    "messages": [
      {
        "role": "user",
        "content": "Reply with one short greeting."
      }
    ]
  }'</code></pre>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
```

See the Docker quickstart for [startup troubleshooting]($link.page('llmd/quickstart').ref('troubleshooting')),
the [CLI reference]($link.page('llmd/cli')) for more flags, and
[Deployment]($link.page('operations/deployment')) for pinned images and readiness checks.
